# Tablet of Discovery's restricted {R}{R} pays for instant and sorcery spells only (CR 106.6): not a creature spell and not
# an activated ability. The Mountain's {R} casts the first Blazing Rootwalla (the creature control); then, with only the
# restricted {R}{R} floating, the second Rootwalla cannot be cast and the first one's "{R}: +2/+0" cannot be activated.
# The Tablet is tapped first, so both are floating when the Rootwalla is cast: its {R} is the Mountain's.
# On turn 3 the Tablet's other ability, an unrestricted {R}, pays for that activation (the control for the ability).

